==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Kaijin Doge]]s spawn after 3.33 seconds<sup>100f</sup>, delay 13.33~20 seconds<sup>400f~600f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Shibalien]]s spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 26.67~33.33 seconds<sup>800f~1,000f</sup>.
*1 [[Malizabeth]] spawns after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>.
*1 [[Madam Peng]] spawns after 33.33 seconds<sup>1,000f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Commander Ostromeda]] spawns as the boss.
**4 [[Malizabeth]]s spawn, delay 33.33~40 seconds<sup>1,000f~1,200f</sup>.
**Infinite [[Aku Doge]]s spawn after 4.67 seconds<sup>140f</sup>, delay 20~26.67 seconds<sup>600f~800f</sup>.
**3 [[Aku Gory|Aku Gories]] spawn after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>, delay 53.33~60 seconds<sup>1,600f~1,800f</sup>.
**4 [[Madam Peng]]s spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 40~46.67 seconds<sup>1,200f~1,400f</sup>.

==Strategy==
Commander Ostromeda demands you collect all [[Anti-unstarred Alien Treasures]] from Into the Future Chapter 1, 2, & 3 to properly deal with him. Your entire lineup should be made with the intent of countering him specifically, which means 3 meatshields and many long range attackers. Specifically, [[Gross Cat (Normal Cat)|Macho Leg Cat]] is a strong choice thanks to his Strong Against Alien ability letting him survive many hits and dish out good damage. Outside of that, [[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|Dual]] [[Crazed Lizard Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Dragons]] can be used to great effect, since the hefty peons supply you with ample cash. You do want [[Giga-Nyan Rex (Uber Rare Cat)|Giga-Nyan Prime DX]] to nuke the Kaijin—specifically Malizabeth—out of existence.

It's not going to be an easy battle, as few good crowd-controlling options exist that outrange Commander Ostromeda. [[Battle Items#Rich Cat|Rich Cat]] is recommended, and you should stall as much as you can at the beginning to build yourself massive momentum later on.

